      "Choose Open viewer to read a file page by page, with zoom, Go to sheet and Switch revision. Add markup or Draw rectangle marks an area: give it a title, assignee, status and comments, and attach it to an issue, RFI, bid package, clarification or VE item under Attached to. Markups stay with the revision they were drawn on.",
      "Sheets is the Drawing log: every drawing sheet at its current version, as a grid or a list, with the discipline filter, search and Changed in. A sheet's pills show all its versions; Revised in (the set) or New says where the current one came from, and Current from gives its set and date.",
      "Sheets are matched by sheet number across every upload, and A-101, A101 and a-101 are the same sheet. Upload a set that holds only the revised sheets: those become the next version and every other sheet stays current.",
      "Choose Add revision on a sheet to upload one PDF page as its next version, even when its title block reads differently. Choose Compare to see two versions side by side; Zoom both pages keeps them aligned.",
      "Sets timeline lists every drawings upload, oldest to newest, with what it revised and added. Choose a set to show only the sheets it changed.",
      "After a drawings upload, Upload check shows how many sheets were revised, new and unchanged. Name sheets lets you type the number of any page whose title block could not be read (Needs a number), and Repeated number flags a number found twice. Looks right closes it; the upload is already stored.",
