      "Choose Add scope item, or an item's pencil, to write the description, source reference, notes, and origin. Saving a change sends an approved item back to Needs review.",
      "Use the circle beside an item to approve or reopen it. Approve visible form approves every draft item in the selected bid form.",
      "For an approved requirement, choose Add to estimate in Requirement detail. Open estimate drafts takes you to Quantity takeoffs; open that trade's Scope drafts to enter a measured quantity, unit and rate. Queueing a responsibility adds no invented quantities or costs.",
      "In Requirement detail, choose Move trade to hand an item to another trade; it returns to review and that trade's owner is notified. Apply to all trades puts one item, such as dust protection, in every trade's bid form.",
      "Upload documents once in Project files. Proposed scope lines appear directly inside their trade. Use Accept, Reject, Move trade or Delete beside each proposal; there is no separate AI findings tab or second upload.",
      "Search the trade list and inspect each proposal’s cited document and page before accepting it. Drawing and quantity proposals appear alongside scope proposals with their own type labels.",
      "Accept adds the scope requirement to the approved bid form. Reject leaves a rejected line that can be restored; Delete hides a proposal while retaining its source and rejection in the audit. General, above all trades, adds common requirements to every bid form with one click; review those items before publishing.",
      "When every item is approved, choose Publish to subcontractors. If the form changes afterwards the package shows Revised, and Publish revision releases the new version.",
      "Open the Section coverage tab to check every section of the project manual against the bid forms (Divisions 00 and 01 are handled in General). Show sections starts on Open questions: Unassigned, Multiple trades and Conflict. Search by section number or title, and expand a row to read why, the suggested trade and Open manual at its pages. Unassigned means check whether the section applies; it is not a confirmed omission.",
      "For each open section, choose Assign to a trade, Record split or Mark not applicable. Assign to a trade shows what it affects before Confirm assignment (a published bid form stays as issued until you republish; an awarded trade's Exhibit A does not change) and adds one draft line citing the section and its pages, for review in Bid forms; assigning again adds nothing. Record split names each trade and its part of the work (supply, installation, firestopping) and Save split records it. Mark not applicable needs a Reason. Undo decision removes either. A decision that no longer matches the bid forms shows Conflict and moves to the top.",
